      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JULIE KEEPING (7) has a fair record and proved too classy last time to win by half a length at Gawler in a handy 22.97 beating Skate In Paris. Well placed and will be tough to beat. LARNI LOU (1) is having her first start around this course. In the money last start when third (23.32) at Gawler over 400m. Has performed well from this box with a win and two minor placings to her name from five starts. Expected to feature again. WYHOON (2) has been a little hard to follow, finishing out of the placings latest but was in winning form two back scoring in a Grade 6 at Gawler. This looks easier and expected to improve sharply. CANYA FEEL IT (8) drops in trip and is not to be underestimated.",
